\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Let evaerlasting glories crown
\par Thy head, my Saviour and my Lord;
\par Thy hands have brought salvation down,
\par And writ the blessing in Thy word.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. In vain  our trembling concience seeks
\par Some  solid ground to rest upon;
\par With long despair our  spirit breaks,
\par Till we apply to Thee alone.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. How well Thy blessed truths agree;
\par How wise and holy Thy commands;
\par Thy promises, how firm they be;
\par How firm our hope and comfort stands!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Should all the forms that men devise
\par Assault my ways with treacherous art,
\par I'd call them vanity and lies,
\par And bind Thy gospel to my heart.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

